IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc18-tracking.l4 -- the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, sections 492.1 and 492.2 (warrants for a tracking device and for a transmission data recorder:
-- who may issue them, what they authorize, how long they are valid, where they may be executed, and the definitions). Part agent ccc18; layer 1. The section 2 terms
-- (public officer, criminal organization, terrorism offence, superior court of criminal jurisdiction) and the computer program of subsection 342.1(2) are taken as
-- MAYBE BOOLEAN inputs; the offences of sections 467.11 to 467.13 are tested by section number (rule R1). A "may" function whose "if" gate fails answers NOTHING
-- (ruling of 2026-11-12 (1)); a validity period that is too long answers JUST FALSE ("as long as"); a definition that says "means" answers JUST FALSE outside it.
-- See the header of `ccc18-soira-notice` and NOTES.md.

§ `Sections 492.1 and 492.2 -- Tracking device and transmission data recorder warrants`

-- src:10913 | Period of validity
-- src:10914 | (5) Subject to subsection (6), a warrant is valid for the period specified in it as long as that period ends no more than 60 days after the day on which the warrant is issued.
@ref Criminal Code s 492.1(5) (src:10913-10914)
GIVEN d IS A DATE, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 492.1(5) the day a number of days after the day` MEANS Date (DATE_DAY d PLUS n) (DATE_MONTH d) (DATE_YEAR d)

@ref Criminal Code s 492.1(5) (src:10913-10914)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 492.1(6) one year after the day` MEANS Date (DATE_DAY d) (DATE_MONTH d) (DATE_YEAR d PLUS 1)   -- the same date a year later (a 29 February rolls to 1 March: NOTES.md, fork F3)

§ `492.1 Warrant for tracking device`

-- src:10905 | Warrant for tracking device — transactions and things
-- src:10906 | 492.1 (1) A justice or judge who is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to suspect that an offence has been or will be committed under this or any other Act of Parliament and that tracking the location of one or more transactions or the location or movement of a thing, including a vehicle, will assist in the investigation of the offence may issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer or a public officer to obtain that tracking data by means of a tracking device.
@ref Criminal Code s 492.1(1) (src:10905-10906)
DECLARE `s 492.1(1) action` IS ONE OF `s 492.1(1) issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer or a public officer to obtain tracking data by means of a tracking device`

@ref Criminal Code s 492.1(1) (src:10905-10906)
GIVEN `the issuer is a justice or a judge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the justice or judge is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to suspect that an offence has been or will be committed under this or any other Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the justice or judge is satisfied that tracking the location of one or more transactions or the location or movement of a thing, including a vehicle, will assist in the investigation of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the warrant authorizes a peace officer or a public officer to obtain that tracking data by means of a tracking device` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 492.1(1) the justice or judge may issue a warrant for a tracking device` MEANS
    IF `the issuer is a justice or a judge` AND `the justice or judge is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to suspect that an offence has been or will be committed under this or any other Act of Parliament` AND `the justice or judge is satisfied that tracking the location of one or more transactions or the location or movement of a thing, including a vehicle, will assist in the investigation of the offence` AND `the warrant authorizes a peace officer or a public officer to obtain that tracking data by means of a tracking device`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer or a public officer to obtain that tracking data by means of a tracking device"

@ref Criminal Code s 492.1(1) (src:10905-10906)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 492.1(1) action`
`s 492.1(1) the power of the justice or judge to issue the warrant` MEANS
    PARTY `a justice`
    MAY `s 492.1(1) issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer or a public officer to obtain tracking data by means of a tracking device`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:10907 | Warrant for tracking device — individuals
-- src:10908 | (2) A justice or judge who is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe that an offence has been or will be committed under this or any other Act of Parliament and that tracking an individual’s movement by identifying the location of a thing that is usually carried or worn by the individual will assist in the investigation of the offence may issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer or a public officer to obtain that tracking data by means of a tracking device.
@ref Criminal Code s 492.1(2) (src:10907-10908)
DECLARE `s 492.1(2) action` IS ONE OF `s 492.1(2) issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer or a public officer to obtain tracking data about an individual by means of a tracking device`

@ref Criminal Code s 492.1(2) (src:10907-10908)
GIVEN `the issuer is a justice or a judge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the justice or judge is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe that an offence has been or will be committed under this or any other Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the justice or judge is satisfied that tracking an individual’s movement by identifying the location of a thing that is usually carried or worn by the individual will assist in the investigation of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the warrant authorizes a peace officer or a public officer to obtain that tracking data by means of a tracking device` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 492.1(2) the justice or judge may issue a warrant for a tracking device, for an individual` MEANS
    IF `the issuer is a justice or a judge` AND `the justice or judge is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe that an offence has been or will be committed under this or any other Act of Parliament` AND `the justice or judge is satisfied that tracking an individual’s movement by identifying the location of a thing that is usually carried or worn by the individual will assist in the investigation of the offence` AND `the warrant authorizes a peace officer or a public officer to obtain that tracking data by means of a tracking device`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer or a public officer to obtain that tracking data by means of a tracking device"

@ref Criminal Code s 492.1(2) (src:10907-10908)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 492.1(2) action`
`s 492.1(2) the power of the justice or judge to issue the warrant` MEANS
    PARTY `a justice`
    MAY `s 492.1(2) issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer or a public officer to obtain tracking data about an individual by means of a tracking device`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:10909 | Scope of warrant
-- src:10910 | (3) The warrant authorizes the peace officer or public officer, or a person acting under their direction, to install, activate, use, maintain, monitor and remove the tracking device, including covertly.
@ref Criminal Code s 492.1(3) (src:10909-10910)
DECLARE `s 492.1(3) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 492.1(3) install the tracking device`
    `s 492.1(3) activate the tracking device`
    `s 492.1(3) use the tracking device`
    `s 492.1(3) maintain the tracking device`
    `s 492.1(3) monitor the tracking device`
    `s 492.1(3) remove the tracking device`
    `s 492.1(3) any other act`

@ref Criminal Code s 492.1(3) (src:10909-10910)
GIVEN act IS A `s 492.1(3) act`
      `it is done by the peace officer or public officer, or a person acting under their direction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is done covertly` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 492.1(3) the warrant authorizes the act` MEANS
    IF NOT `it is done by the peace officer or public officer, or a person acting under their direction`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The warrant authorizes the peace officer or public officer, or a person acting under their direction"
    ELSE CONSIDER act
         WHEN `s 492.1(3) any other act` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the warrant authorizes "to install, activate, use, maintain, monitor and remove the tracking device, including covertly"
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE   -- the listed acts, "including covertly" (`it is done covertly` does not change the answer)

-- src:10911 | Conditions
-- src:10912 | (4) A warrant may contain any conditions that the justice or judge considers appropriate, including conditions to protect a person’s interests.
@ref Criminal Code s 492.1(4) (src:10911-10912)
GIVEN `the justice or judge considers the condition appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 492.1(4) the warrant may contain the condition` MEANS
    IF `the justice or judge considers the condition appropriate`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A warrant may contain any conditions that the justice or judge considers appropriate"

-- src:10913 | Period of validity
-- src:10914 | (5) Subject to subsection (6), a warrant is valid for the period specified in it as long as that period ends no more than 60 days after the day on which the warrant is issued.
@ref Criminal Code s 492.1(5) (src:10913-10914)
GIVEN `the day on which the warrant is issued` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the period specified in the warrant ends` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 492.1(5) the warrant is valid for the period specified in it` MEANS
    IF `the day on which the period specified in the warrant ends` AT MOST `s 492.1(5) the day a number of days after the day` `the day on which the warrant is issued` 60
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a warrant is valid for the period specified in it as long as that period ends no more than 60 days after the day on which the warrant is issued"

-- src:10915 | Period of validity — organized crime and terrorism offence
-- src:10916 | (6) A warrant is valid for the period specified in it as long as that period ends no more than one year after the day on which the warrant is issued, if the warrant relates to
-- src:10917 | (a) an offence under any of sections 467.11 to 467.13;
-- src:10918 | (b) an offence committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with a criminal organization; or
-- src:10919 | (c) a terrorism offence.
@ref Criminal Code s 492.1(6) (src:10915-10919)
GIVEN `the day on which the warrant is issued` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the period specified in the warrant ends` IS A DATE
      `(a) the warrant relates to an offence under any of sections 467.11 to 467.13` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `(b) the warrant relates to an offence committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with a criminal organization` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(c) the warrant relates to a terrorism offence, by s 2 terrorism offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 492.1(6) the warrant is valid for the period specified in it, for organized crime and terrorism offences` MEANS
    IF `the day on which the period specified in the warrant ends` GREATER THAN `s 492.1(6) one year after the day` `the day on which the warrant is issued`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A warrant is valid for the period specified in it as long as that period ends no more than one year after the day on which the warrant is issued"
    ELSE IF (`(a) the warrant relates to an offence under any of sections 467.11 to 467.13`'s `section` AT LEAST 467.11 AND `(a) the warrant relates to an offence under any of sections 467.11 to 467.13`'s `section` AT MOST 467.13) OR `(b) the warrant relates to an offence committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with a criminal organization`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE CONSIDER `(c) the warrant relates to a terrorism offence, by s 2 terrorism offence`
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the longer period is for a warrant that "relates to (a) an offence under any of sections 467.11 to 467.13; (b) an offence committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with a criminal organization; or (c) a terrorism offence"
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "terrorism offence" is defined in section 2, answered by the keel

-- src:10920 | Execution in Canada
-- src:10921 | (6.1) A warrant issued under this section may be executed at any place in Canada. Any public officer or peace officer who executes the warrant must have authority to act in that capacity in the place where the warrant is executed.
@ref Criminal Code s 492.1(6.1) (src:10920-10921)
GIVEN `the place is in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 492.1(6.1) (place) the warrant may be executed at the place` MEANS
    IF `the place is in Canada`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A warrant issued under this section may be executed at any place in Canada"

-- src:10920 | Execution in Canada
-- src:10921 | (6.1) A warrant issued under this section may be executed at any place in Canada. Any public officer or peace officer who executes the warrant must have authority to act in that capacity in the place where the warrant is executed.
@ref Criminal Code s 492.1(6.1) (src:10920-10921)
GIVEN `the public officer or peace officer who executes the warrant has authority to act in that capacity in the place where the warrant is executed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 492.1(6.1) (officer) the officer who executes the warrant has the authority the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the public officer or peace officer who executes the warrant has authority to act in that capacity in the place where the warrant is executed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any public officer or peace officer who executes the warrant must have authority to act in that capacity in the place where the warrant is executed"

-- src:10922 | Removal after expiry of warrant
-- src:10923 | (7) On ex parte application supported by an affidavit, the justice or judge who issued a warrant or another justice or judge who has jurisdiction to issue such warrants may authorize the covert removal of the tracking device after the expiry of the warrant under any conditions that the justice or judge considers advisable in the public interest. The authorization is valid for the period specified in it as long as that period is not more than 90 days.
@ref Criminal Code s 492.1(7) (src:10922-10923)
GIVEN `the application is ex parte and supported by an affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the justice or judge is the one who issued the warrant or another justice or judge who has jurisdiction to issue such warrants` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the warrant has expired` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conditions are ones that the justice or judge considers advisable in the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 492.1(7) the justice or judge may authorize the covert removal of the tracking device after the expiry of the warrant` MEANS
    IF `the application is ex parte and supported by an affidavit` AND `the justice or judge is the one who issued the warrant or another justice or judge who has jurisdiction to issue such warrants` AND `the warrant has expired` AND `the conditions are ones that the justice or judge considers advisable in the public interest`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may authorize the covert removal of the tracking device after the expiry of the warrant under any conditions that the justice or judge considers advisable in the public interest"

-- src:10922 | Removal after expiry of warrant
-- src:10923 | (7) On ex parte application supported by an affidavit, the justice or judge who issued a warrant or another justice or judge who has jurisdiction to issue such warrants may authorize the covert removal of the tracking device after the expiry of the warrant under any conditions that the justice or judge considers advisable in the public interest. The authorization is valid for the period specified in it as long as that period is not more than 90 days.
@ref Criminal Code s 492.1(7) (src:10922-10923)
GIVEN `the number of days in the period specified in the authorization` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 492.1(7) the authorization is valid for the period specified in it` MEANS
    IF `the number of days in the period specified in the authorization` AT MOST 90
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The authorization is valid for the period specified in it as long as that period is not more than 90 days"

§ `492.1(8) Definitions`

-- src:10924 | Definitions
-- src:10925 | (8) The following definitions apply in this section.
-- src:10926 | data means representations, including signs, signals or symbols, that are capable of being understood by an individual or processed by a computer system or other device. (données)
@ref Criminal Code s 492.1(8) (src:10924-10926)
GIVEN `it is a representation, including signs, signals or symbols` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is capable of being understood by an individual or processed by a computer system or other device` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 492.1(8) "data" data` MEANS
    IF `it is a representation, including signs, signals or symbols` AND `it is capable of being understood by an individual or processed by a computer system or other device`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "data means representations, including signs, signals or symbols, that are capable of being understood by an individual or processed by a computer system or other device"

-- src:10927 | judge means a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction or a judge of the Court of Quebec. (juge)
@ref Criminal Code s 492.1(8) (src:10927-10927)
GIVEN `the person is a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction, by s 2 superior court of criminal jurisdiction` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is a judge of the Court of Quebec` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 492.1(8) "judge"` MEANS
    IF `the person is a judge of the Court of Quebec` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE CONSIDER `the person is a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction, by s 2 superior court of criminal jurisdiction`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "judge means a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction or a judge of the Court of Quebec"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "superior court of criminal jurisdiction" is defined in section 2, answered by the keel

-- src:10928 | public officer means a public officer who is appointed or designated to administer or enforce a federal or provincial law and whose duties include the enforcement of this or any other Act of Parliament. (fonctionnaire public)
@ref Criminal Code s 492.1(8) (src:10928-10928)
GIVEN `the person is a public officer, by s 2 public officer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is appointed or designated to administer or enforce a federal or provincial law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person’s duties include the enforcement of this or any other Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 492.1(8) "public officer"` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the person is appointed or designated to administer or enforce a federal or provincial law`) OR (NOT `the person’s duties include the enforcement of this or any other Act of Parliament`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "public officer means a public officer who is appointed or designated to administer or enforce a federal or provincial law and whose duties include the enforcement of this or any other Act of Parliament"
    ELSE `the person is a public officer, by s 2 public officer`   -- JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE ("means a public officer"); NOTHING when the keel's answer is not covered

-- src:10929 | tracking data means data that relates to the location of a transaction, individual or thing. (données de localisation)
@ref Criminal Code s 492.1(8) (src:10929-10929)
GIVEN `it is data, as defined in this subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it relates to the location of a transaction, individual or thing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 492.1(8) "tracking data" tracking data` MEANS
    IF `it is data, as defined in this subsection` AND `it relates to the location of a transaction, individual or thing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "tracking data means data that relates to the location of a transaction, individual or thing"

-- src:10930 | tracking device means a device, including a computer program within the meaning of subsection 342.1(2), that may be used to obtain or record tracking data or to transmit it by a means of telecommunication. (dispositif de localisation)
@ref Criminal Code s 492.1(8) (src:10930-10930)
GIVEN `it is a device` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a computer program within the meaning of subsection 342.1(2), by s 342.1(2) computer program` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it may be used to obtain or record tracking data or to transmit it by a means of telecommunication` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 492.1(8) "tracking device"` MEANS
    IF NOT `it may be used to obtain or record tracking data or to transmit it by a means of telecommunication`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "tracking device means a device, including a computer program within the meaning of subsection 342.1(2), that may be used to obtain or record tracking data or to transmit it by a means of telecommunication"
    ELSE IF `it is a device` THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE CONSIDER `it is a computer program within the meaning of subsection 342.1(2), by s 342.1(2) computer program`
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "tracking device means a device, including a computer program within the meaning of subsection 342.1(2)"
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "computer program" is defined in subsection 342.1(2), answered by another part

§ `492.2 Warrant for transmission data recorder`

-- src:10931 | Warrant for transmission data recorder
-- src:10932 | 492.2 (1) A justice or judge who is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to suspect that an offence has been or will be committed against this or any other Act of Parliament and that transmission data will assist in the investigation of the offence may issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer or a public officer to obtain the transmission data by means of a transmission data recorder.
@ref Criminal Code s 492.2(1) (src:10931-10932)
DECLARE `s 492.2(1) action` IS ONE OF `s 492.2(1) issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer or a public officer to obtain transmission data by means of a transmission data recorder`

@ref Criminal Code s 492.2(1) (src:10931-10932)
GIVEN `the issuer is a justice or a judge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the justice or judge is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to suspect that an offence has been or will be committed against this or any other Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the justice or judge is satisfied that transmission data will assist in the investigation of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the warrant authorizes a peace officer or a public officer to obtain the transmission data by means of a transmission data recorder` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 492.2(1) the justice or judge may issue a warrant for a transmission data recorder` MEANS
    IF `the issuer is a justice or a judge` AND `the justice or judge is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to suspect that an offence has been or will be committed against this or any other Act of Parliament` AND `the justice or judge is satisfied that transmission data will assist in the investigation of the offence` AND `the warrant authorizes a peace officer or a public officer to obtain the transmission data by means of a transmission data recorder`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer or a public officer to obtain the transmission data by means of a transmission data recorder"

@ref Criminal Code s 492.2(1) (src:10931-10932)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 492.2(1) action`
`s 492.2(1) the power of the justice or judge to issue the warrant` MEANS
    PARTY `a justice`
    MAY `s 492.2(1) issue a warrant authorizing a peace officer or a public officer to obtain transmission data by means of a transmission data recorder`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:10933 | Scope of warrant
-- src:10934 | (2) The warrant authorizes the peace officer or public officer, or a person acting under their direction, to install, activate, use, maintain, monitor and remove the transmission data recorder, including covertly.
@ref Criminal Code s 492.2(2) (src:10933-10934)
DECLARE `s 492.2(2) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 492.2(2) install the transmission data recorder`
    `s 492.2(2) activate the transmission data recorder`
    `s 492.2(2) use the transmission data recorder`
    `s 492.2(2) maintain the transmission data recorder`
    `s 492.2(2) monitor the transmission data recorder`
    `s 492.2(2) remove the transmission data recorder`
    `s 492.2(2) any other act`

@ref Criminal Code s 492.2(2) (src:10933-10934)
GIVEN act IS A `s 492.2(2) act`
      `it is done by the peace officer or public officer, or a person acting under their direction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 492.2(2) the warrant authorizes the act` MEANS
    IF NOT `it is done by the peace officer or public officer, or a person acting under their direction`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The warrant authorizes the peace officer or public officer, or a person acting under their direction"
    ELSE CONSIDER act
         WHEN `s 492.2(2) any other act` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the warrant authorizes "to install, activate, use, maintain, monitor and remove the transmission data recorder, including covertly"
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:10935 | Limitation
-- src:10936 | (3) No warrant shall be issued under this section for the purpose of obtaining tracking data.
@ref Criminal Code s 492.2(3) (src:10935-10936)
GIVEN `the purpose of the warrant is to obtain tracking data` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 492.2(3) no warrant shall be issued under this section` MEANS
    IF `the purpose of the warrant is to obtain tracking data`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No warrant shall be issued under this section for the purpose of obtaining tracking data"

-- src:10937 | Period of validity
-- src:10938 | (4) Subject to subsection (5), a warrant is valid for the period specified in it as long as that period ends no more than 60 days after the day on which the warrant is issued.
@ref Criminal Code s 492.2(4) (src:10937-10938)
GIVEN `the day on which the warrant is issued` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the period specified in the warrant ends` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 492.2(4) the warrant is valid for the period specified in it` MEANS
    IF `the day on which the period specified in the warrant ends` AT MOST `s 492.1(5) the day a number of days after the day` `the day on which the warrant is issued` 60
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a warrant is valid for the period specified in it as long as that period ends no more than 60 days after the day on which the warrant is issued"

-- src:10939 | Period of validity — organized crime or terrorism offence
-- src:10940 | (5) The warrant is valid for the period specified in it as long as that period ends no more than one year after the day on which the warrant is issued, if the warrant relates to
-- src:10941 | (a) an offence under any of sections 467.11 to 467.13;
-- src:10942 | (b) an offence committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with a criminal organization; or
-- src:10943 | (c) a terrorism offence.
@ref Criminal Code s 492.2(5) (src:10939-10943)
GIVEN `the day on which the warrant is issued` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the period specified in the warrant ends` IS A DATE
      `(a) the warrant relates to an offence under any of sections 467.11 to 467.13` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `(b) the warrant relates to an offence committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with a criminal organization` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(c) the warrant relates to a terrorism offence, by s 2 terrorism offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 492.2(5) the warrant is valid for the period specified in it, for organized crime and terrorism offences` MEANS
    IF `the day on which the period specified in the warrant ends` GREATER THAN `s 492.1(6) one year after the day` `the day on which the warrant is issued`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The warrant is valid for the period specified in it as long as that period ends no more than one year after the day on which the warrant is issued"
    ELSE IF (`(a) the warrant relates to an offence under any of sections 467.11 to 467.13`'s `section` AT LEAST 467.11 AND `(a) the warrant relates to an offence under any of sections 467.11 to 467.13`'s `section` AT MOST 467.13) OR `(b) the warrant relates to an offence committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with a criminal organization`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE CONSIDER `(c) the warrant relates to a terrorism offence, by s 2 terrorism offence`
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the longer period is for a warrant that "relates to (a) an offence under any of sections 467.11 to 467.13; (b) an offence committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with a criminal organization; or (c) a terrorism offence"
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "terrorism offence" is defined in section 2, answered by the keel

-- src:10944 | Execution in Canada
-- src:10945 | (5.1) A warrant issued under subsection (1) may be executed at any place in Canada. Any public officer or peace officer who executes the warrant must have authority to act in that capacity in the place where the warrant is executed.
@ref Criminal Code s 492.2(5.1) (src:10944-10945)
GIVEN `the place is in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 492.2(5.1) (place) the warrant may be executed at the place` MEANS
    IF `the place is in Canada`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A warrant issued under subsection (1) may be executed at any place in Canada"

-- src:10944 | Execution in Canada
-- src:10945 | (5.1) A warrant issued under subsection (1) may be executed at any place in Canada. Any public officer or peace officer who executes the warrant must have authority to act in that capacity in the place where the warrant is executed.
@ref Criminal Code s 492.2(5.1) (src:10944-10945)
GIVEN `the public officer or peace officer who executes the warrant has authority to act in that capacity in the place where the warrant is executed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 492.2(5.1) (officer) the officer who executes the warrant has the authority the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the public officer or peace officer who executes the warrant has authority to act in that capacity in the place where the warrant is executed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any public officer or peace officer who executes the warrant must have authority to act in that capacity in the place where the warrant is executed"

§ `492.2(6) Definitions`

-- src:10946 | Definitions
-- src:10947 | (6) The following definitions apply in this section.
-- src:10948 | data means representations, including signs, signals or symbols, that are capable of being understood by an individual or processed by a computer system or other device. (données)
@ref Criminal Code s 492.2(6) (src:10946-10948)
GIVEN `it is a representation, including signs, signals or symbols` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is capable of being understood by an individual or processed by a computer system or other device` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 492.2(6) "data" data` MEANS
    IF `it is a representation, including signs, signals or symbols` AND `it is capable of being understood by an individual or processed by a computer system or other device`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "data means representations, including signs, signals or symbols, that are capable of being understood by an individual or processed by a computer system or other device"

-- src:10949 | judge means a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction or a judge of the Court of Quebec. (juge)
@ref Criminal Code s 492.2(6) (src:10949-10949)
GIVEN `the person is a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction, by s 2 superior court of criminal jurisdiction` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is a judge of the Court of Quebec` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 492.2(6) "judge"` MEANS
    IF `the person is a judge of the Court of Quebec` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE CONSIDER `the person is a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction, by s 2 superior court of criminal jurisdiction`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "judge means a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction or a judge of the Court of Quebec"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "superior court of criminal jurisdiction" is defined in section 2, answered by the keel

-- src:10950 | public officer means a public officer who is appointed or designated to administer or enforce a federal or provincial law and whose duties include the enforcement of this or any other Act of Parliament. (fonctionnaire public)
@ref Criminal Code s 492.2(6) (src:10950-10950)
GIVEN `the person is a public officer, by s 2 public officer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is appointed or designated to administer or enforce a federal or provincial law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person’s duties include the enforcement of this or any other Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 492.2(6) "public officer"` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the person is appointed or designated to administer or enforce a federal or provincial law`) OR (NOT `the person’s duties include the enforcement of this or any other Act of Parliament`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "public officer means a public officer who is appointed or designated to administer or enforce a federal or provincial law and whose duties include the enforcement of this or any other Act of Parliament"
    ELSE `the person is a public officer, by s 2 public officer`

-- src:10951 | transmission data means data that
-- src:10952 | (a) relates to the telecommunication functions of dialling, routing, addressing or signalling;
-- src:10953 | (b) is transmitted to identify, activate or configure a device, including a computer program as defined in subsection 342.1(2), in order to establish or maintain access to a telecommunication service for the purpose of enabling a communication, or is generated during the creation, transmission or reception of a communication and identifies or purports to identify the type, direction, date, time, duration, size, origin, destination or termination of the communication; and
-- src:10954 | (c) does not reveal the substance, meaning or purpose of the communication. (données de transmission)
@ref Criminal Code s 492.2(6) (src:10951-10954)
GIVEN `it is data, as defined in this subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(a) it relates to the telecommunication functions of dialling, routing, addressing or signalling` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(b) it is transmitted to identify, activate or configure a device, including a computer program as defined in subsection 342.1(2), in order to establish or maintain access to a telecommunication service for the purpose of enabling a communication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(b) it is generated during the creation, transmission or reception of a communication and identifies or purports to identify the type, direction, date, time, duration, size, origin, destination or termination of the communication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(c) it reveals the substance, meaning or purpose of the communication` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 492.2(6) "transmission data"` MEANS
    IF `it is data, as defined in this subsection` AND `(a) it relates to the telecommunication functions of dialling, routing, addressing or signalling`
       AND (`(b) it is transmitted to identify, activate or configure a device, including a computer program as defined in subsection 342.1(2), in order to establish or maintain access to a telecommunication service for the purpose of enabling a communication`
            OR `(b) it is generated during the creation, transmission or reception of a communication and identifies or purports to identify the type, direction, date, time, duration, size, origin, destination or termination of the communication`)
       AND (NOT `(c) it reveals the substance, meaning or purpose of the communication`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "transmission data means data that (a) relates to the telecommunication functions of dialling, routing, addressing or signalling"

-- src:10955 | transmission data recorder means a device, including a computer program within the meaning of subsection 342.1(2), that may be used to obtain or record transmission data or to transmit it by a means of telecommunication. (enregistreur de données de transmission)
@ref Criminal Code s 492.2(6) (src:10955-10955)
GIVEN `it is a device` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a computer program within the meaning of subsection 342.1(2), by s 342.1(2) computer program` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it may be used to obtain or record transmission data or to transmit it by a means of telecommunication` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 492.2(6) "transmission data recorder"` MEANS
    IF NOT `it may be used to obtain or record transmission data or to transmit it by a means of telecommunication`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "transmission data recorder means a device, including a computer program within the meaning of subsection 342.1(2), that may be used to obtain or record transmission data or to transmit it by a means of telecommunication"
    ELSE IF `it is a device` THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE CONSIDER `it is a computer program within the meaning of subsection 342.1(2), by s 342.1(2) computer program`
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "transmission data recorder means a device, including a computer program within the meaning of subsection 342.1(2)"
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "computer program" is defined in subsection 342.1(2), answered by another part
